  "_comment": "Vendor/product -> technology-category -> industries taxonomy. This is the signal that catches intelligence like 'Critical vulnerability in Atlassian's Rovo AI' without the source ever saying 'Technology sector' -- see server/industryClassification.js#matchTechnologyIndustries/matchVendorProductIndustries. The MECHANISM (category -> industries) is the reusable part; the vendor list below is deliberately extensible seed data, same 'curated list, not NLP, extend via this file' convention as industry-map-21.json. `specificity: narrow` categories are used by a specific, identifiable set of industries (a category-match there produces tier TECHNOLOGY_RELEVANT); `specificity: broad` categories are used by essentially any organization regardless of sector (a category-match there produces the weaker tier POTENTIALLY_EXPOSED against every industry in its `industries` list -- deliberately not 'all 21', see each category's own `industries`). Vendor/product keywords are matched case-insensitively as whole-word/leading-boundary substrings against free text (article title+summary) OR checked directly against a CVE's own vendor/product fields (server/lib/cpe.js's already-parsed CPE vendor/product) -- see matchVendorProductIndustries for the latter, which never needs the free-text regex at all.",
